    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0700" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/9–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-02T18:00:00-04:00">October 2, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1045. ReEmbs 1457 [<hi rendition="#italic">1437</hi>], September 1.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d655-f1"/> Department is informed by Navy and War Departments that
                    October 9 is satisfactory date to Commander, Panama Sea Frontier,<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d655-f2"/> and to General Brett<anchor n="44" xml:id="d655-f3"/> for
                    initiating staff conversations with Chile. Please ascertain from Chilean
                    Government whether this date is satisfactory and if so make appropriate advance
                    arrangements. On receipt of your telegraphic reply officers will be assigned by
                    War and Navy Departments to begin the conversations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="42" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it indicated Chile’s acceptance of staff conversations (810.20
                    Defense /9–144).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f2" n="43" xml:id="d655-f2-content">
                <p>Capt. Ellis S. Stone.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f3" n="44" xml:id="d655-f3-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. George H. Brett, Commanding General, Caribbean Defense Command.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
